# The build context is an allowlist: everything is excluded, and only what the
# image needs is re-admitted below.
#
# This is not tidiness. The working tree holds fetched Orders and HawkExpress
# invoice PDFs — customer freight records — alongside virtual environments,
# database dumps and logs. A denylist is one forgotten directory away from
# baking those into an image layer, permanently and irretrievably. With this
# shape, a directory added later is excluded until somebody deliberately
# admits it.
*

# The service itself.
!dwb
!dwb/**
!viewer.py

# Its Python dependencies, installed from the lockfile.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock

# Its frontend, built in the Node stage from the lockfile.
!frontend
!frontend/**

# ...but never the frontend's installed tree or a build made on the host: both
# are large, both are platform-specific, and the image builds its own.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/node_modules/**
frontend/dist
frontend/dist/**

# Nor anything Python leaves lying around inside an admitted directory.
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.py[cod]
